BlockerFlow public lists
https://github.com/khaleel-git/blockerflow-lists

This repository republishes the two block lists that ship with BlockerFlow. Both are
built from third-party sources and from BlockerFlow's own additions. This file names each
source, its licence, where its terms are published, and which files here derive from it.

Last checked: 2026-11-19.


1. LICENCE BY FOLDER
--------------------

  pornography/    GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0). Full text: LICENSE
  web-proxy/      Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0).
                  Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt
  everything else (README.md, manifest.json, blockerflow_public_key.pem, tooling):
                  GPL-3.0, same as pornography/

Why two licences:

  - pornography/ combines data from sources under the Unlicense, the MIT licence and
    GPL-3.0 (OISD and HaGeZi). The Unlicense and MIT terms allow reuse under GPL-3.0, and
    GPL-3.0 requires the combined work to be GPL-3.0. No CC BY-SA text is copied into this
    folder. keyword_tiers.txt only uses CC BY-SA word-frequency lists to choose a label for
    BlockerFlow's own keywords (section 2.7), and CC BY-SA 4.0 material may be relicensed under
    GPL-3.0 in any case.
  - web-proxy/ is built from the UT1 "redirector" list, which is CC BY-SA 4.0. Share-alike
    requires the derived list to stay CC BY-SA 4.0 (or a licence Creative Commons lists as
    compatible). It contains no GPL-3.0 data, so there is nothing that forces GPL there.

BlockerFlow's own work (the curated additions, the keyword files, the build) is released
under the licence of the folder it sits in. Copyright (c) 2026 BlockerFlow (khaleel-git).


