2.6 BlockerFlow's own work, and files derived from the sources above
    Every file under pornography/ other than the four domain files is listed here, with
    where it comes from. All of them are GPL-3.0, like the rest of pornography/.

    pornography/keywords.txt
        BlockerFlow's own weighted keyword list. Not taken from any source above.
    pornography/keywords_intl.txt
        BlockerFlow's own multilingual adult keyword list. Not taken from any source above.
        Wikipedia article titles were scanned to test it; none are copied into the file.
    pornography/keyword_tiers.txt
        Labels (strong or context) for BlockerFlow's own keywords from keywords.txt. A script
        sets them from explicit word stems BlockerFlow chose, the adult brand roots (below), and
        word-frequency lists (section 2.7) and words found in links on the home pages of the
        most popular sites (a test set built from the Tranco list, section 2.8) used to find
        common words. The file lists BlockerFlow's keywords only; nothing is copied from those
        inputs, and no Tranco hostnames or ranks are published here.
    pornography/adult_hostname_keywords.txt
        Brand roots derived from the domain list: a script takes the registrable label of every
        domain in domains.txt, keeps roots that all four sources (2.1 to 2.4) list across at least
        20 domains, and a person reviews them. It is therefore derived from the pornography/
        sources 2.1 to 2.4 and is GPL-3.0 on the same terms. A set of legitimate domains is used
        only to check that no root blocks them; none of those domains are copied.
    The few web-proxy hosts BlockerFlow added by hand are CC BY-SA 4.0, like the rest of
    web-proxy/.

